# Claims
```json
[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/gates/junit.ts",
  "line": 145,
  "title": "Freshness: compare the report with a filesystem timestamp, not Date.now()",
  "detail": "Linux CI fails the six 'covering JUnit requires fresh exact testcase evidence' cases. `mtimeMs < startedAt` compares filesystem time with `Date.now()` (run.ts ~163), and on Linux a just-written report's mtime can lag the wall clock. Review reproduced it on macOS by subtracting 10 ms from `mtimeMs`. Fix: before launching the command, create a fresh sentinel file on the report's filesystem (beside the report path, in the factory's scratch) and use its `statSync().mtimeMs` as the baseline. Make the test fixture use the same kind of filesystem baseline. Keep the absent-path and no-follow checks. Add a test that simulates a filesystem clock lagging the wall clock."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/harness/sandbox.ts",
  "line": 392,
  "title": "Put the factory's reporter arguments where a template's `--` can't make them positional",
  "detail": "The factory appends `--reporter=junit --reporter-outfile=...` after the template's arguments. A `retry_files` template ending in `--` turns them into positional file arguments, so no report is written. That fails closed today, but it makes every such repository silently unable to bind. Either insert the factory's reporter and filter arguments before any `--` in the parsed template, or refuse a covering request at configuration time when the template contains `--`, with a clear reason. Test both forms."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/pipeline/gate-evidence.ts",
  "line": 174,
  "title": "Refuse a `met` row whose covering citation has no factory record",
  "detail": "#915's test 3 requires that a verifier output asserting `met` with a made-up covering citation stays unaccepted. `applyGateEvidence` returns existing `met` rows unchanged (~174), and verification.ts ~104 then derives an overall pass. Review reproduced a schema-parsed `met` row with a fabricated covering citation and no factory record producing `overall: \"pass\"`. The existing test at gate-evidence.test.ts ~1405 expects that status to survive: change it. Fix: any row whose evidence or `gateEvidence` claims a factory or covering-test citation is accepted only if it matches a factory record for the same SHA. Otherwise downgrade it to blocked, with the reason."
 },
 {
  "id": "F4",
  "file": "src/pipeline/covering-tests.ts",
  "line": 101,
  "title": "State the in-process reporter residual in a code comment and the issue's out of scope",
  "detail": "Review showed that the code under test can forge or replay its own JUnit report: it can write the XML to `LIMITLESS_GATE_REPORT` and exit before Bun does. Bun's reporter runs in the same process as the tests, so no file check can authenticate it. The orchestrator accepts this as a residual: it is the same trust the existing 'tests pass' gate places in the test run's exit status, and review of the tests is the defence. Add a short comment at the binding saying so. No mechanism change for this."
 }
